## 🧠 What I Learned

1. **Prompt engineering for complex apps** — Breaking the build into MVP → Enhanced forces clearer thinking about core vs nice-to-have features
2. **Single-file HTML is powerful** — A full SaaS-quality app with zero dependencies (except Chart.js CDN) fits in one file
3. **Nutrition data complexity** — Indian food databases (IFCT 2017) differ significantly from USDA; using the right source matters
4. **Iterative AI development** — Prompt 1 gave a working foundation; Prompt 2 layered on top cleanly without breaking anything
5. **Chart.js with dark themes** — Requires explicit color overrides for axes, labels, and grids; defaults are for light mode

